meta {
  name: Review queue
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/imports/records?status=NeedsReview
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffToken}}
}

docs {
  What the import pipeline could not decide by itself.

  Two kinds of thing land here. A **field** question — most often `RIGHTS_UNKNOWN`, meaning no
  policy exists for that source and somebody must take responsibility before republishing
  somebody else's words. And a **match** question — `FUZZY_MATCH` or `AMBIGUOUS_MATCH`, where a
  listing looks like an existing product. Attaching it to the wrong one rewrites something
  customers are already buying, so near-ties are never resolved automatically.

  Approving does not publish: it makes the record valid and the next pipeline step picks it up.
  So clearing a hundred records does not mean waiting on a hundred round trips.
}
